{"text": "Achebe-Whitlow & Sato, CPAs, P.A.\n6100 Uptown Blvd NE, Suite 420, Albuquerque, NM 87110\n\nPhone 505-555-0136 · Fax 505-555-0137 · www.awscpa.example\n\nMarch 18, 2026\n\nInternal Revenue Service\n\nOgden, UT 84201-0038\n\nRe: Request for abatement of failure-to-deposit penalty\n\nTaxpayer: Three Sisters Tamales LLC\n\nEIN: 85-1440927\n\nTax form and period: Form 941, quarter ended March 31, 2025\n\nNotice: CP276B dated February 9, 2026\n\nPenalty assessed: $4,317.82\n\nTo whom it may concern:\n\nWe represent the taxpayer named above under the enclosed Form 2848 (CAF no.\n0314-88271-R). On the taxpayer's behalf we respectfully request abatement of the\nfailure-to-deposit penalty assessed under IRC § 6656 for the first quarter of 2025,\non the grounds of reasonable cause and, in the alternative, under the first-time\nabatement policy in IRM 20.1.1.3.2.\n\nFacts. Three Sisters is a family restaurant and wholesale kitchen with eleven\nemployees. Its sole managing member, María José Fernández de Córdoba (SSN\nending 4099), personally handled every payroll tax deposit from the company's\nformation in 2019 through January 2025, and every deposit in that period was\nmade on time and in full.\n\nOn February 11, 2025 Ms. Fernández de Córdoba suffered an ischemic stroke at\nwork and was admitted to Presbyterian Rio Grande Medical Center. She remained\nan inpatient until March 6, 2025 and was then in inpatient rehabilitation for\naphasia until April 22, 2025. During that period she could not speak on the\n\ntelephone, read numbers reliably, or use a computer. A letter from her treating\nneurologist is enclosed.\n\nNo one else at the company had access to the electronic deposit system. Her\ndaughter, Luz Fernández, kept the kitchen open and paid the employees by\nhandwritten check, but did not know that deposits were due. The semiweekly\ndeposits for the pay dates between February 14 and March 28, totalling\n$31,609.44, were therefore not made when due.\n\nCorrection. As soon as Ms. Fernández de Córdoba was able to review the mail,\nthe company deposited the full amount on April 29, 2025, filed the return on time,\nand engaged Sandia Crest Payroll Co. to make all future deposits. Every deposit\nsince has been timely. The company has no penalties in the prior three years.\n\nRequest. The taxpayer exercised ordinary business care and prudence and was\nprevented from complying by the sudden, serious illness of the only person\nresponsible. We ask that the penalty of $4,317.82 and the related interest be\nabated in full. My direct line is (505) 555-0139 and my email address is\ndachebe@awscpa.example if you need anything further.\n\nRespectfully,\n\nDesmond Achebe-Whitlow, CPA\n\nNew Mexico license no. CPA-7714 · PTIN P01847733\n\nEnclosures: Form 2848; physician letter; deposit confirmations\n\ncc: M. J. Fernández de Córdoba, 412 Atrisco Vista Rd SW, Albuquerque, NM 87121", "kind": "PDF", "detail": "2 pages · 447 words", "notes": [], "names": {"people": ["María José Fernández de Córdoba", "Luz Fernández", "Ms. Fernández de Córdoba", "Desmond Achebe-Whitlow"], "companies": ["Achebe-Whitlow & Sato, CPAs, P.A.", "Three Sisters Tamales LLC", "Presbyterian Rio Grande Medical Center", "Sandia Crest Payroll Co.", "awscpa"]}, "topics": {"places": ["Albuquerque", "Rio Rancho"], "health": ["ischemic stroke", "aphasia"], "sensitive": ["María José Fernández de Córdoba", "luz Fernández", "race or ethnicity"], "names": ["María José", "Luz", "Desmond", "M. J.", "Fernández de Córdoba", "Achebe-Whitlow"]}, "judged": {"candidates": 0, "requests": 0, "failures": 0, "places": [], "labels": {}}, "chunks": 2, "chunkErrors": 0, "topicErrors": 0, "importMs": 228.69999999552965, "modelMs": 0, "topicMs": 0, "detectors": ["email", "url", "ip", "iban", "card", "card_exp", "cvv", "ssn", "bn_ca", "sin_ca", "ein", "card_partial", "phone", "street", "dob", "age90", "date", "passport_dl", "routing", "credential", "device", "vin", "record", "account", "money", "zi